=Below are {{ $json.messageCount }} messages from {{ $json.channelCount }} team channel(s) over the last {{ $('Standup Config').first().json.LookbackHours }} hours.

{{ $json.combinedText }}

Messages that matched the blocker keywords:
{{ $json.keywordBlockerText }}

Turn this into a standup digest. Only use what is actually in the messages - if a section has nothing, return an empty array for it rather than inventing entries. Attribute to a person where the message makes it clear.

Return ONLY raw JSON, no code fences, no commentary:
{"shipped": ["short line per thing completed"], "blockers": ["short line per blocker, naming who is blocked and on what"], "nextUp": ["short line per thing planned next"], "needsAttention": true or false}

needsAttention is true if anything here genuinely needs a lead to step in today - someone blocked with no path forward, a missed deadline, or an unresolved incident. Routine work in progress is not needsAttention.

